WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.133
-Cailee, welcome to the show.
I'm so excited that you're here.

00:00:03.133 --> 00:00:04.334
Not only because
I loved your performance,

00:00:04.334 --> 00:00:07.400
but this is your first
talk-show appearance.

00:00:07.400 --> 00:00:09.033
-It's my first one.
-Ever.

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:12.801
I'm so happy
to be your first talk-show host.

00:00:12.801 --> 00:00:14.033
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:17.067
I want to know all about you.
We all do.

00:00:17.067 --> 00:00:19.067
We'll talk about "Priscilla"
and what a great job.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.334
But where are you from?

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:22.801
Where is this --
Where does it all start?

00:00:22.801 --> 00:00:24.634
-I was born in Tennessee

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:26.868
and I was raised
in Southern Missouri.

00:00:26.868 --> 00:00:28.234
-Yeah.

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.200
-Sheryl's actually
from Southern Missouri, too,

00:00:30.200 --> 00:00:31.434
so shout-out
to the Missouri girls tonight.

00:00:31.434 --> 00:00:34.734
-Yeah, doing pretty well.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:37.267
Were you musical growing up?

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:40.100
-Yeah, I sort of did
a bunch of different things.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.667
I did, like, musical theater
and I was in a kids cover band.

00:00:45.667 --> 00:00:47.467
-Ooh! Tell me about that.

00:00:47.467 --> 00:00:53.234
-Yeah. Well, we were
called Energy, but capital NRG,

00:00:53.234 --> 00:00:55.000
which is really hardcore.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:58.734
-Really cool. Yeah, NRG.
-NRG. Do you get it?

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:01.067
I don't know if you do,
-No, but now I do, yeah.

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:04.534
Do you guys get it?
NRG, Energy?

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:06.167
Where would you play?

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:08.334
-We'd do, like, all --
We'd do, you know,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.834
Halloween parties,
birthday parties,

00:01:10.834 --> 00:01:13.133
some fall festivals, you know.

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:14.501
-You could book NRG,
and they would come

00:01:14.501 --> 00:01:15.601
and they would just do
all the hits.

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:16.767
-All the hits.

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:19.901
We did Joan Jett,
Pat Benatar, Pink Floyd,

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.868
you know, depending on what
the mood was the night --

00:01:21.868 --> 00:01:23.334
-How cool were these kids
you were playing for?

00:01:23.334 --> 00:01:24.968
I mean, this is --
-Yeah, we were pretty --

00:01:24.968 --> 00:01:27.334
-Pink Floyd?
-Yeah. Yeah, we were cool kids.

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:29.868
Yeah, I did -- Actually, like,
I played at a fall festival,

00:01:29.868 --> 00:01:34.534
and that's where I got
my sort of ticket to L.A.

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:36.834
It was like this guy
came up to me, and he was like,

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:39.868
"I've got a Myspace band,
and I know someone who knows

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:42.300
someone who's a manager in L.A."

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:45.334
I'm like, "Great!
-"I have a Myspace band"?

00:01:45.334 --> 00:01:47.667
-Yeah. I'm like,
"Let's pack the bag."

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.634
-And you were like,
"This is my big break, Mom."

00:01:49.634 --> 00:01:52.667
-Yeah. And we did. We packed
the bags, and my mom --

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:54.234
-You believed this man.

00:01:54.234 --> 00:01:56.834
-I mean, yeah.
That was my only way in.

00:01:56.834 --> 00:01:59.133
-This man got you
where you are today.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:00.334
-Yeah.
-No way.

00:02:00.334 --> 00:02:01.634
-I know.

00:02:01.634 --> 00:02:04.334
-From his Myspace band
that he thought that -- Wow!

00:02:04.334 --> 00:02:07.234
-He really helped me out.
So, we went on the journey.

00:02:07.234 --> 00:02:10.234
It was like a 25-hour
cross-country drive.

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:12.901
And it was a wild, wild ride.

00:02:12.901 --> 00:02:16.133
-Did you plan on doing music in
L.A. or acting or both?

00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.467
-Just anything.
I was like, "I'm your girl."

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:21.767
-Yeah. "I can do it.
I can do it all." Yeah.

00:02:21.767 --> 00:02:25.067
And then you end up getting --
you get "Priscilla."

00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:26.801
-Yeah, so crazy.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:29.167
I mean, Sofia Coppola
was my dream director.

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:30.767
-She's the coolest.
-Yeah.

00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:32.100
-I would get nervous
around just even

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:33.133
hanging out with her,
seeing Sofia Coppola.

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:36.234
-Oh, gosh,
she's so chic and chill.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:39.234
And she just --
She's just so -- She's so fun.

00:02:39.234 --> 00:02:41.367
-She's we kind of --
In your head, you go,

00:02:41.367 --> 00:02:42.667
"Oh, she's kind of like
a perfect --

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:43.834
just cool and does everything."

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.834
I go, "What would
surprise me about Sofia?"

00:02:45.834 --> 00:02:47.534
-Yeah. Yeah.
-And you brought me a photo.

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:48.834
-This surprised me, as well.

00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:51.167
-Yeah. She plays pickleball.

00:02:51.167 --> 00:02:56.167
-In between -- This was in prep.
She painted a pickleball court.

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:58.234
Also, we had 30 days
to shoot this movie,

00:02:58.234 --> 00:03:00.100
which is not a lot of time,

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:03.067
but we still found time
to play pickleball.

00:03:03.067 --> 00:03:04.634
We ended up --
-There's you and Jacob.

00:03:04.634 --> 00:03:05.767
-This is a tournament.

00:03:05.767 --> 00:03:08.701
It ended up turning into
a whole tournament,

00:03:08.701 --> 00:03:10.601
which she, of course, won.

00:03:10.601 --> 00:03:12.334
You know, we worked hard
and we played hard.

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:14.100
That's that's how she does it.
-Exactly.

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.467
-The Sofia Coppola way.
-She's the coolest.

00:03:16.467 --> 00:03:17.601
-She is the coolest.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.934
-And you got to go
to Venice Film Festival.

00:03:19.934 --> 00:03:22.367
-Yeah, yeah. We were
lucky enough to go to Venice.

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:24.334
-And you got
a crazy standing ovation.

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:27.434
Everyone loved your performance.
But here's what I want to hear.

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:28.767
You go in,
you sit down in your seat,

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.767
and who sits next to you?

00:03:30.767 --> 00:03:32.901
-Yeah, so, it's my first time

00:03:32.901 --> 00:03:36.801
at the Venice Film Festival,
and it's this --

00:03:36.801 --> 00:03:39.133
It's like what you think of
in your dreams.

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:40.367
You know,
it's a massive festival.

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:43.534
-Red carpet, paparazzi.
-Yeah, it's unbelievable.

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:46.067
And I hadn't seen the film yet,
because I was just so nervous

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:49.200
to watch myself on-screen
for two hours in every frame.

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.701
Like, I don't know anyone
who wants to do that.

00:03:51.701 --> 00:03:52.934
-I do.
-Oh, you do?

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:54.734
-Yeah. You're really good.
You're really good.

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:56.667
Yeah, you're very good.

00:03:56.667 --> 00:03:59.234
-So, yeah, we got there,
and I --

00:03:59.234 --> 00:04:01.200
The whole plan was that
they were going to sneak me out

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:06.734
during the show and I was going
to come back for the ending.

00:04:06.734 --> 00:04:08.901
And then I turned to Sofia
at the last minute.

00:04:08.901 --> 00:04:11.133
I'm like, "I don't know.
What do you think I should do?"

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:13.167
And she's like,
"This is a really special night.

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:15.501
I think you should
watch the movie."

00:04:15.501 --> 00:04:16.634
I'm like, "Okay, yeah, great.

00:04:16.634 --> 00:04:18.167
I'm not going to say
no to Sofia."

00:04:18.167 --> 00:04:20.467
And then I sit down,
and Priscilla Presley --

00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:23.067
They sat me right next
to Priscilla Presley.

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:26.033
So I'm watching --
-That's the best.

00:04:26.033 --> 00:04:27.868
That's exactly what you want.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:31.934
-Most out-of-body experience
of my life.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:33.167
-Well, also, what do you do?

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.434
Do you watch your performance
or do you watch

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:36.634
Priscilla's reaction
to your, like, performance?

00:04:36.634 --> 00:04:40.033
"I'm playing you."
-Jacob was right in between us.

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.667
So I would go,
"Jacob, how's it looking?"

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:44.234
-Like, "Dude,
make a break for it.

00:04:44.234 --> 00:04:46.234
She does not like it."
Yeah.

00:04:46.234 --> 00:04:47.367
But she loved it.

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:48.801
-Yeah, it's the first time
she turned to me,

00:04:48.801 --> 00:04:51.267
and she said that she liked
the performance

00:04:51.267 --> 00:04:53.634
and she got to watch her life
through the movie,

00:04:53.634 --> 00:04:54.834
which is, like,
the best review you can --

00:04:54.834 --> 00:04:57.100
-Did you get to interview her
before you did --

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.901
-Yeah, yeah, I got to spend
some time with her,

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:04.934
which was wild, you know,
growing up an Elvis fan.

00:05:04.934 --> 00:05:09.200
You know, we did road trips to
Graceland with the family.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.534
-It must be surreal.
-So surreal.

00:05:10.534 --> 00:05:12.634
You know, I had all
these questions planned out,

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:14.000
getting ready to meet her,

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.567
but then Priscilla Presley
walks in through the doors,

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:18.567
and everything goes out
of your head.

00:05:18.567 --> 00:05:20.400
I couldn't get words out
of my mouth.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.267
-Yeah, you're like, "W-W-W-What
is rock 'n' roll?"

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:25.601
"What? What is rock 'n' roll?"

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:27.434
-Like, staring at the table,
and she, like, sat down

00:05:27.434 --> 00:05:30.501
and she's like, "So, do you want
to ask me any questions?"

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:32.868
I was like, "Uh, yeah, right."
-"We should do that, yeah."

00:05:32.868 --> 00:05:34.167
-"We should do that.
That's a great idea."

00:05:34.167 --> 00:05:35.667
-But did she say, like,
any, like --

00:05:35.667 --> 00:05:37.000
And you don't have to
say it here,

00:05:37.000 --> 00:05:39.100
but, like, any, like,
moments that you go like,

00:05:39.100 --> 00:05:41.267
"Wow, that's kind of an intimate
moment between you and Elvis."

00:05:41.267 --> 00:05:43.000
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:44.300
Yeah, her eyes would,
like, light up.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.801
Like, she went back
to those moments.

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:48.734
I remember one she told me,
which was so touching.

00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:50.734
She -- When she first went to
the party

00:05:50.734 --> 00:05:52.167
to meet Elvis
for the first night,

00:05:52.167 --> 00:05:54.434
she was so hungry
because she was --

00:05:54.434 --> 00:05:55.767
She just couldn't eat all day.

00:05:55.767 --> 00:05:57.167
She was so nervous
to go to the party.

00:05:57.167 --> 00:06:01.234
And then she went,
she saw him, and he was, like,

00:06:01.234 --> 00:06:02.834
making her a sandwich.

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:04.801
And he's like,
"Do you want a sandwich?"

00:06:04.801 --> 00:06:06.534
And she was like,
"I can't eat a sandwich

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:08.367
in front of Elvis Presley."

00:06:08.367 --> 00:06:11.200
She's like, "There's no way."
-He made her a sandwich?

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.801
-Yeah.
-That's fantastic.

00:06:12.801 --> 00:06:13.834
I love stories like that.

00:06:13.834 --> 00:06:15.634
-I know.
-That's so wild.

00:06:15.634 --> 00:06:17.467
You're great in this movie.
-Thanks for saying that.

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:18.868
-Congratulations.
No, it's awesome.

00:06:18.868 --> 00:06:20.133
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:20.133 --> 00:06:21.467
Here's Cailee Spaeny
in "Priscilla."

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:22.567
Take a look.

00:06:24.767 --> 00:06:26.968
-What do you think? You like it?

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:29.701
-I love it.
I can't believe you did this.

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:32.667
[ Laughs ]

00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:34.767
-Alright, it's time to go.
Scilla's graduating.

00:06:34.767 --> 00:06:37.634
-Can I ask you something?

00:06:37.634 --> 00:06:42.367
I was wondering if maybe you
could wait outside the ceremony,

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:44.501
'cause I'm afraid you being
there might take away

00:06:44.501 --> 00:06:47.534
the attention
from the graduates.

00:06:47.534 --> 00:06:50.167
-Well, yeah, I-I guess
I hadn't -- I hadn't

00:06:50.167 --> 00:06:53.467
thought of it like that.

00:06:53.467 --> 00:06:55.801
I-I won't come in.

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:59.234
I'll, uh -- I'll wait for you
outside in the car.

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:01.834
In a way,
it'll kind of be like I'm there.

00:07:03.234 --> 00:07:04.767
-Thank you.

00:07:04.767 --> 00:07:07.000
-Come on.
Cailee Spaeny, everyone!

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:11.067
"Priscilla" is in theaters
nationwide tomorrow.

00:07:11.067 --> 00:07:12.501
More "Tonight Show"
after the break.

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:13.767
Stick around.
Come back, please.

00:07:13.767 --> 00:07:14.801
-Okay.

